Describe a mine as connected physical, informational, and working systems (@mine-system: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2", #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #source "../sources/CETEM-Usinas-de-Beneficiamento.lingua#r_62ZD994C9YYXB1YDVFQST5B27J", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Material-grade-recovery-and-operating-vocabulary.lingua#r_0BXGZZP1DEME655JAC89NJ6A4J") { r_0WEGJD1A06ZDDW1CMPYCCZE9G6
**Read:** [Introduction to Mining Engineering — Penn State MNG 230](../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2), the whole public introductory course progressively; [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the complete lifecycle/layout and environmental context; [Usinas de Beneficiamento de Minérios do Brasil — CETEM](../sources/CETEM-Usinas-de-Beneficiamento.lingua#r_62ZD994C9YYXB1YDVFQST5B27J), one complete integrated case initially, then the whole book.

A mine includes exploration/evaluation, access and development, extraction, material handling, processing, waste/water systems, maintenance, and closure/post-closure. These stages overlap and change the conditions encountered later. Closure assumptions affect early layout and material choices rather than appearing only after production ends.

Draw stocks, flows, equipment, work, information, utilities, and decision boundaries. Ore and waste are classifications within a specified plan and context; the same material may change destination when quality, processing, geometry, or constraints change. Preserve the physical material identity through those decisions.

Interfaces matter: a plant feed requirement influences selective mining and stockpiles, excavation affects ground/ventilation, dewatering changes water pathways, and maintenance or workforce constraints limit usable capacity. A nominal equipment rate does not describe the throughput of the connected system.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete published teaching/plant case as a lifecycle and process account. Name the inputs/outputs and the teams exchanging samples, material, data, or responsibility. Identify one dependency whose loss changes several downstream systems and trace how the effect would be observed.

Read the entire introductory course and revisit its system map through the later studies. The source books provide substantial explanations; these Records connect their quantities, assumptions, and practical consequences without introducing another Lince abstraction or requiring every neighboring field before starting.

**Continue:** [Keep mining and processing terms tied to their quantities and contexts](Material-grade-recovery-and-operating-vocabulary.lingua#r_0BXGZZP1DEME655JAC89NJ6A4J).

